From 59dbef0cdbd73ed29e12d5072fda9963a44ae899 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Mostovoy <stavultras@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 07:33:39 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] hw/arm/filogic, hw/mips/mt7621: flash chips by type and ID

The flash options become flash-type (nand, nor, emmc; MT7621: nor,
parallel-nand), flash-id, flash-mb, flash-uid and, for SPI-NOR +
SPI-NAND boards, flash2-id / flash2-mb / flash2-uid (the other type);
dump-dir replaces nand-dir.  nand, nor, flash, nand-id, nor-id,
nand-uid, nor-uid and nor-nand are gone.

One table (flash_chips.h) gives the size of a known chip from its type
and ID; an ID that is not listed needs flash-mb, a size that differs
from the listed one is an error.  The type is never taken from the ID.
Without flash-id the first chip of the type is used (W25N01GV,
W25Q128JV, K9F1G08U0D), as before.  The flash-id help is built from the
table.  flash-uid of a SPI-NOR is taken as Cudy firmware shows it (the
bytes reversed) on both machines.

